<title>UK: UK electric companies seek windfall tax instalment.</title>
<headline>UK electric companies seek windfall tax instalment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's electricity companies have made a last ditch effort to avert the impact of the windfall tax with a letter to Chancellor Gordon Brown, Sunday Business said.</p>
<p>The Electricity Association, which represents Britain's suppliers and generators, has pleaded for electricity companies to be allowed to pay their share of the windfall tax, which could be as high as 10 billion stg, in instalments, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The power businesses want a staggered payment schedule so that they could manage their case effectively over the tax period, it said.</p>
<p>((--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106))</p>
